(ver 3.1.1, as an Elf)
1. Polymorphing:  Early in what is proving to be my greatest game ever the
first two rings I found were, much to my delight, polymorph and poly control.
I was having a wild old time transforming into a vampire lord and master lich,
but I noticed problems:
	a.  It didn't always work.  Sometimes it would fail and I would 
revert to elf-dom, but I assume this is normal.  But what is it based upon?  
What's the formula?
	b.  (This is the big one)  I noticed that my stats, especially my
experience, bouncing all around the board.  My strength dropped from 18/02 
(from spinach) down to 16, and I jumped from level to level.  Mostly at 
first it was negative, but eventually I got some positive levels.  One time
I was lucky enough to bounce up to lv.17 from what I think would have been
about 9.  So I quit polymorphing and restored my strength (and was lucky
enough to get dex18 from (I think) polymorphing to boot).
	So my questions are:
		(1)  Is this normal?  I mean, for the game to just double 
your levels like this?  Quite a spoiler...
		(2)  If I start polymorphing again, do I run the risk of 
losing all these bonus levels?  From excessively bad luck I haven't found
a way across water and I'd love to polymorph into a dragon for some Ludios
looting (that's right, no WoC, no boots, no ring, not a single potion,
nothing in 20 levels).

2. Temple Donations:  I know that you can get good stuff by donating large 
chunks of money to priests and I certainly have the cash.  I know that it 
starts at 40xLevel and is fickle, but what is the actual breakdown about
what one can get.  My god is just jumping up and down happy with me, and 
I have Stormy.

	And speaking of temples, when I recently prayed (looking for holy
water) my god shouted out something like "You have been chosen to steal
souls for me!"  What exactly does this mean, and what can I do with it?

	On an interesting side note, the level I'm currently on had an
altar, a clear potion, a fountain, and a wand of create monster all in
the same room.  I was amused. 
